Thank you to RedHatCat.
The solution was not about re-creating, but moving the device you end up
with, back to what you require.

I'd been fiddling with dsfmgr -e (for exchange) which requires both units to
exist.
dsfmgr -m (for move) tapeX tape0 did the trick. 

This will presumably also be handy for other devices such as disks or
network interface devices. 

