Boot from CD Installation disk
     boot cdrom=5Fdevice  (Example  b dka500)
Go to Unix Shell
Make your special devices
     cd  /dev
     =2E/MAKEDEV system=5Fdisk tape=5Fdrive  (ex=3A =2E/MAKEDEV rz0 tz15)=

Make filedomain and file sets for  root
     mkfdmn  =96r  =96t  rz  /dev/rz0a  root=5Fdomain
     mkfset  root=5Fdomain  root
Restore root
     mount  =96t  advfs  root=5Fdomain=23root  /mnt
     cd   /mnt
     vrestore  -xvf  /dev/nrmt0h   (make sure the tape is aligned)
     cd / =

Make some adjustments
     mkdir  =96p   /mnt/etc/fdmns/root=5Fdomain
     mkdir  =96p   /mnt/etc/fdmns/usr=5Fdomain
     ln  =96s   /dev/rz0a   /mnt/etc/fdmns/root=5Fdomain/rz0a
     ln  =96s   /dev/rz0g   /mnt/etc/fdmns/root=5Fdomain/rz0g
     cd   /mnt/etc
     vi  fstab
          add  root=5Fdomain=23root   /     advfs  rw   1 0
          add  usr=5Fdomain=23usr     /usr  advfs  rw   1 0
          comment the old lines for root and usr or remove them
          cd  /
     umount  /mnt
Make file domain and file sets for /usr
     mkfdmn  =96r  =96t  rz  /dev/rz0g  usr=5Fdomain
     mkfset  usr=5Fdomain  usr
Restore usr
     mount  =96t  advfs  usr=5Fdomain=23usr  /mnt
     cd   /mnt
     vrestore  -xvf  /dev/nrmt0h  (make sure the tape is aligned)
     cd / =


Boot system



