-----Original Message-----
From: Jan Mark Holzer [mailto:jmh@hp.com]
Sent: lundi, 18. novembre 2002 13:54
To: 'McGuinness Todd'
Subject: RE: Applications on TruCluster 5.1A



Hi Todd,

	this should not be a problem as ORACLE will detect the instance
being
	active (on the other node).
	When ORACLE starts it creates a lock file for the instance and
in
	a TruCluster environment this file is cluster wide (ie. common
	ORACLE_HOME). If you try to start up the second instance it
	will fail with an error message. All which would happen is that
	the ORACLE processes are started but not DB files are opened .
	I haven't tried it in a while but that's how it should work :).

Hth,

	Jan

 


