I found the GNU install to be a battle of cc errors when doing configure and
make.  An easier path was finding a compiled binary on the media :

Compaq Tru64UNIX Version 5.1A, Open Source Software Collection, RPM Install

(I was hoping to pull it off a Compaq url but couldn't find it)

It's the Red Hat Package Manager.  Executing 2 commands

	/mnt/SETUP/RPM-init.ksh
	/mnt/SETUP/install-grep-2.4.2-4.ksh

installed the GNU grep in /usr/local/bin/ .

