We're trying to configure our Tru64 Unix workstation (a Compaq Alpha 264DP 
that is a couple years old) to use DHCP.  We're using V5.0A of the 
operating system, and until recently we weren't using DHCP but instead 
giving it a user supplied value for the local machine IP address.  Changes 
were made to the network over the summer and we're now being told we must 
use DHCP to assign our IP address.  We have discovered that when we choose 
the "Use DHCP" option in the Network Setup wizard the program inserts the 
word DYNAMIC in the IP address field.  When we click OK we get the Error 
Message saying that the word DYNAMIC is invalid.  Does anyone have any idea 
of how to fix this or how we get around this problem (or even what is going 
on here)?
